{%- comment -%}
  Outputs the storefront sign-in URL.

  When a logged-in landing page is configured (settings.customer_logged_in_url),
  the URL carries a return_to pointing at the /pages/login-redirect router page,
  which then forwards the customer to that account page after login.

  Must use the /customer_authentication/login endpoint — the /account/login
  endpoint drops return_to with new customer accounts.

  Renders no value other than the URL (safe to use inside href="" and as a filter
  argument).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if settings.customer_logged_in_url != blank
    assign return_path = '/pages/login-redirect' | url_encode
    echo '/customer_authentication/login?return_to=' | append: return_path
  else
    echo routes.account_login_url
  endif
-%}
